.TH OROC-TOOLING-CPP 1 "" "Oro Runtime 0.2.1" "Oro Runtime Manual"
.SH NAME
oroc\-tooling\-cpp \- Export C, C++, Objective\-C and Objective\-C++ compiler commands.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
oroc tooling cpp [options] [<project\-dir>]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Export C, C++, Objective\-C and Objective\-C++ compiler commands.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-platform=<name>\fR
desktop, linux, mac, win, android, ios or ios\-simulator
.TP
\fB\-\-arch=<name>\fR
target architecture (host by default; arm64 for Android/iOS)
.TP
\fB\-\-prod\fR
select release compiler flags
.TP
\fB\-\-prepare\fR
build explicitly configured CMake preparation targets
.TP
\fB\-\-refresh\fR
allocate a fresh editor generation
.TP
\fB\-\-offline\fR
disable CMake FetchContent downloads and updates
.TP
\fB\-\-config=<path>\fR
use an explicit oro.toml or oro.ini
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
show help
.SH NOTES
.PP
Uses Oro extension declarations, an existing compilation database, or a configured CMake project.
.PP
Generated commands target original source files and live under build.output/.oro\-tooling.
.PP
Apple SDK discovery requires macOS and Xcode; Android requires the selected NDK.
.PP
Custom scripts and generated dependency headers require a build\-system compilation database or CMake provider.
.PP
See docs/LANGUAGE_SERVER.md for configuration and editor examples.
.SH SEE ALSO
oroc(1), oroc\-tooling(1)
